{"shortDescription":"MANAGEMENT REPORTNordic Fibreboard AS consolidated net revenue in Q2 2026 was €2.27 million, representing a 21.4% increase compared to the same period of the previous year (Q2 2025: €1.87 million), revenue increased by €397 thousand. The Group's main business activity is the production and wholesal…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["MANAGEMENT REPORT"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Nordic Fibreboard AS consolidated net revenue in Q2 2026 was €2.27 million, representing a 21.4% increase compared to the same period of the previous year (Q2 2025: €1.87 million), revenue increased by €397 thousand. The Group's main business activity is the production and wholesale of fibreboard, which accounted for the vast majority of the Group's revenue in Q2 2026. The second segment comprises the management of the property located on Suur-Jõe Street in Pärnu. However, following the termination of the lease agreements for the building in August 2024, the revenue generated by this segment is immaterial."]},{"type":"p","children":["Nordic Fibreboard's consolidated EBITDA in Q2 2026 was negative €225 thousand, with an EBITDA margin of negative 10% (Q2 2025 EBITDA: negative €94 thousand, EBITDA margin: negative 5%). The results for the Q2 2026 were significantly negatively impacted by the sharp increase in gas prices in February 2026. The negative impact is ongoing, and the company is not able to raise product prices to a level that would match the rise in gas prices. This is partly due to long-term contracts with fixed prices, and partly due to the competitive situation prevailing in the market."]},{"type":"p","children":["Financial expenses in Q2 2026 were €44 thousand, consisting of loan interest costs and other financial costs (€46 thousand in Q2 2025)."]},{"type":"p","children":["The Group's consolidated net loss for Q2 2026 was €414 thousand (Q2 2025 net loss: €268 thousand)."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Fibreboard production and sales"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Revenue from fibreboard sales amounted to €2.27 million in Q2 2026, compared with €1.87 million in the same period of 2025, representing an increase of €397 thousand, or 21.4%. The improvement in sales performance was primarily supported by sales to new customers."]},{"type":"p","children":["Nordic Fibreboard Ltd OÜ’s EBITDA for the Q2 of 2026 was negative EUR 188 thousand (Q2 2025 negative EUR 67 thousand). Nordic Fibreboard Ltd OÜ’s net loss for the Q2 of 2026 amounted to EUR 377 thousand (Q2 2025 net loss of EUR 241 thousand). Q2 2026 EBITDA was negatively impacted by a sharp rise in energy prices (including gas prices nearly doubling), which resulted from the U.S. military strike on Iran at the end of February."]},{"type":"p","children":["Fibreboard sales by geographical segments"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":2},"children":[" ",{"type":"i","children":["€ thousand"]}," "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":2},"children":[" ",{"type":"i","children":["€ thousand"]}," "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" Region "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" ",{"type":"b","children":["Q2 2026"]}," "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" ",{"type":"b","children":["Q2 2025"]}," "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" ",{"type":"b","children":["6m 2026"]}," "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" ",{"type":"b","children":["6m 2025"]}," "]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" European Union "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" 2,154 "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" 1,777 "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" 3,